==========================
Apache POI - DataFormatter Notes
==========================

✔ Purpose:
- Converts any Excel cell value into a String.
- Returns the value exactly as displayed in Excel.

Syntax:
    DataFormatter formatter = new DataFormatter();
    String data = formatter.formatCellValue(cell);

Why use DataFormatter?
✔ No need to check cell type (String, Number, Date, Boolean, Formula).
✔ Prevents formatting issues (e.g., 100 instead of 100.0).
✔ Commonly used in Selenium Excel Utility classes.

Example:
Excel Cell      Returned String
--------------------------------
Sameer          "Sameer"
100             "100"
10.5            "10.5"
12-Aug-2026     "12-Aug-2026"
TRUE            "TRUE"

try-catch:
try {
    data = formatter.formatCellValue(cell);
} catch (Exception e) {
    data = "";
}

✔ Prevents exceptions if the cell is null or empty.
✔ Returns an empty string instead of stopping the program.

Resource Cleanup:
    wb.close();   // Closes Workbook (releases memory)
    fi.close();   // Closes FileInputStream (releases file)

Return:
    return data;  // Returns the formatted cell value as a String.

Interview Answer:
"DataFormatter is used to convert any Excel cell value into a String exactly as it appears in Excel, without manually checking the cell type."